From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wangzlei <66336933+wangzlei@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:02:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] exp: default eBPF config: context_propagation tcp

TCP options only, the same as the obi receiver default: trace context (kind 25)
on requests and service.name (kind 26, adot-obi patch 01) on responses. No HTTP
traceparent header injection, so the application payload is never modified;
RED metrics and peer.service.name topology are unchanged. Same change as adot-obi
config/otel.yaml.
---
 packaging/dependencies/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ebpf.yaml | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packaging/dependencies/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ebpf.yaml b/packaging/dependencies/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ebpf.yaml
index 51206830..7d3ef042 100644
--- a/packaging/dependencies/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ebpf.yaml
+++ b/packaging/dependencies/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ebpf.yaml
@@ -26,8 +26,10 @@ receivers:
     log_level: INFO
     ebpf:
       bpf_fs_base_dir: /sys/fs/bpf
-      # Pinned: cwagent's obi receiver defaults to "tcp".
-      context_propagation: "all"
+      # TCP options only (also cwagent's obi receiver default): trace context
+      # (kind 25) on requests, service.name (kind 26, patch 01) on responses.
+      # No HTTP header injection: the application payload is never modified.
+      context_propagation: "tcp"
       # false (OBI's default): a server request ends when its response is complete.
       # true submits it at the first response write, which dropped ~31% of
       # requests whose downstream calls were slow or timed out (ping demo, 2026-10-09).
-- 
2.50.1

